1
00:00:00,650 --> 00:00:03,655
A delivery vehicle leaves a paper
warehouse.

2
00:00:03,655 --> 00:00:06,659
Every second, a new position mark appears.

3
00:00:06,659 --> 00:00:10,522
The marks are becoming farther apart along
the route.

4
00:00:15,650 --> 00:00:19,480
The positions lift from the road onto a
graph.

5
00:00:19,480 --> 00:00:25,013
Time runs across the bottom. Distance
rises up the side, forming a smooth

6
00:00:25,013 --> 00:00:25,439
curve.

7
00:00:30,650 --> 00:00:33,097
Choose two times and connect their
positions.

8
00:00:33,097 --> 00:00:37,640
The line measures an average speed across
that interval, but the vehicle is

9
00:00:37,640 --> 00:00:38,689
changing its speed.

10
00:00:45,650 --> 00:00:49,834
Hold the two-second position fixed. Move
the other time closer.

11
00:00:49,834 --> 00:00:54,854
Each new line turns slightly, as the
measurement interval becomes shorter and

12
00:00:54,854 --> 00:00:55,272
shorter.

13
00:01:00,650 --> 00:01:03,883
The moving line seems to settle into one
direction.

14
00:01:03,883 --> 00:01:08,913
Its slope offers a way to describe speed
at the target, without measuring zero

15
00:01:08,913 --> 00:01:09,272
time.

16
00:01:15,650 --> 00:01:20,817
The delivery reaches exactly two seconds.
What is its speed at this moment?

17
00:01:20,817 --> 00:01:25,189
Use the nearby position changes to find a
convincing mathematical answer.
